openmediavault-immich (8.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Storage configuration now uses shared folder references
    (sharedFolderSelect dropdowns) instead of plain path inputs: the
    stack files, the photo library and the PostgreSQL data each point
    to a shared folder on the data array. The ctl helper resolves the
    references with omv_get_sharedfolder_path, the Salt state with
    omv_conf.get_sharedfolder_path, and the engine module listens for
    shared folder changes to re-render on Apply.
  * Upgrade note for 8.0.1 installations: re-select the three shared
    folders on the settings page and apply the changes. Existing data
    is not moved automatically -- either create the shared folders at
    the previous locations or migrate the data before starting the
    stack again.
  * Pin the default image version to v3.2.4 (was the floating
    'release' tag) and report 'notinstalled' while the stack files are
    not rendered yet.

 -- fffeng99999  Sun, 04 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Immich photo library management plugin for
    OpenMediaVault 8.x.
    - Settings: version tag, web port, timezone, compose directory,
      upload (photo) location, database location and credentials and
      the optional machine-learning service.
    - Renders .env and docker-compose.yml into the compose directory on
      Apply; deploy/start/stop/restart/upgrade run through
      'docker compose' as background tasks with live output.
    - Live status: container state, running Immich version (server
      API), latest upstream release and update detection, log viewer
      and generated compose file preview.
    - Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations included.

